[{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Evaluate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for each of the following, leaving your answers in exact form:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=x^3-2x^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+2x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\dfrac{x^5-1}{x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sqrt{x}(1-x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=3x^2+2x^{-2},\\qquad f'(2)=12+\\frac12=\\frac{25}{2}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=\\frac12x^{-1/2}+8x^3,\\qquad f'(2)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt2}+64=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}+64.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=x^3-x^{-2},\\quad f'(x)=3x^2+2x^{-3},\\quad f'(2)=12+\\frac14=\\frac{49}{4}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f(x)=x^{1/2}-x^{3/2},\\quad f'(x)=\\frac12x^{-1/2}-\\frac32x^{1/2}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(2)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt2}-\\frac32\\sqrt2=-\\frac{5\\sqrt2}{4}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>For each of the following curves, find the equation of the tangent line which passes through the given point. Give your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by+c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3-x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac1x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(-2,-\\dfrac12\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x,\\qquad \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=2}=4.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-4=4(x-2)\\Rightarrow y-4=4x-8\\Rightarrow 4x-y-4=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2-1,\\qquad \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-5=2(x-1)\\Rightarrow y-5=2x-2\\Rightarrow 2x-y+3=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^{-1}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-x^{-2},\\qquad \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-2}=-\\frac14.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y+\\frac12=-\\frac14(x+2)\\Rightarrow4y+2=-x-2\\Rightarrow x+4y+4=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=2x^{1/2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=x^{-1/2},\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-2=1(x-1)\\Rightarrow y-2=x-1\\Rightarrow x-y+1=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q3","number":3,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the tangent to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3-x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> may be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-k=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a value to be found.</p></li><li><p>Explain the significance of the gradient of this tangent.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-2x,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=0}=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-3=0(x-0)\\Rightarrow y-3=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The gradient is zero, so the curve is neither increasing nor decreasing at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (it is the maximum point of the quadratic).</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>For each of the following curves, find the equation of the normal line which passes through the given point. Give your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by+c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b,c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x^4-x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac1{x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(2,\\dfrac14\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x-x^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=6x,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=6.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-3=-\\frac16(x-1)\\Rightarrow6y-18=-x+1\\Rightarrow x+6y-19=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=20x^3-2x,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-1}=-18.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-4=\\frac1{18}(x+1)\\Rightarrow18y-72=x+1\\Rightarrow x-18y-73=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^{-2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-2x^{-3},\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=2}=-\\frac14.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-\\frac14=4(x-2)\\Rightarrow y-\\frac14=4x-8\\Rightarrow4y-1=16x-32\\Rightarrow16x-4y-31=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^{1/2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac12x^{-1/2},\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=\\frac12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-1=-2(x-1)\\Rightarrow y-1=-2x+2\\Rightarrow2x+y-3=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-1-1=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=1-4x^3,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-1}=5.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y+2=-\\frac15(x+1)\\Rightarrow5y+10=-x-1\\Rightarrow x+5y+11=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>For the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x^2+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=30\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=10x=30\\Rightarrow x=3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>For the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3-2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2-2=10\\Rightarrow x^2=4\\Rightarrow x=\\pm2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>For the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^{1/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac1{4\\sqrt2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac12x^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt2}\\Rightarrow\\sqrt x=2\\sqrt2\\Rightarrow x=8.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac1x+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is shown below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.32/questions/assets/q08.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the equation of the tangent line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p></li><li><p>Find the equation of the normal line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates where the tangent and normal line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> meets the coordinate axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^{-1}+2,\\quad\\frac{dy}{dx}=-x^{-2},\\quad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=-1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-3=-1(x-1)\\Rightarrow y-3=-x+1\\Rightarrow y=-x+4.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-3=1(x-1)\\Rightarrow y-3=x-1\\Rightarrow y=x+2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Tangent line meets axes at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>Normal line meets axes at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3-3x^2+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is shown below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.32/questions/assets/q09.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the equation of the normal line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax+by=c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a,b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates where the normal line crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>Hence calculate the area of the triangle bounded by the normal line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the coordinate axes.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2-6x,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=3}=9.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-2=-\\frac19(x-3)\\Rightarrow9y-18=-x+3\\Rightarrow x+9y=21.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left(0,\\frac73\\right)\\text{ and }(21,0).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times\\frac73\\times21=\\frac{49}{2}=24.5\\text{ units}^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac1x+x^3+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is shown below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.32/questions/assets/q10.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the equation of the tangent line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates where the tangent line crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates where the tangent meets the curve again.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^{-1}+x^3,\\quad\\frac{dy}{dx}=-x^{-2}+3x^2,\\quad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-3=2(x-1)\\Rightarrow y-3=2x-2\\Rightarrow y=2x+1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(-\\frac12,0\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2x+1=\\frac1x+x^3+1\\Rightarrow2x^2+x=1+x^4+x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x^4-2x^2-x+1=0\\Rightarrow(x^2-1)(x^2-1)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow(x-1)^2(x+1)^2=0\\text{ so }x=\\pm1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-1-1=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on the curve</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=5x^2-\\frac1x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>The tangent line to the curve at point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which lies on the curve is parallel to the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y+9x=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the coordinates of the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the other point where the tangent intersects the curve.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=5x^2-x^{-1},\\qquad\\frac{dy}{dx}=10x+x^{-2}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y+9x=5\\Rightarrow y=-9x+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the gradient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"10x+x^{-2}=-9\\Rightarrow10x^3+1=-9x^2\\Rightarrow10x^3+9x^2+1=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow(x+1)(10x^2-x+1)=0\\text{ has solution }x=-1\\text{ so A is }(-1,6).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-6=-9(x+1)\\Rightarrow y=-9x-3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5x^2-x^{-1}=-9x-3\\Rightarrow5x^3-1=-9x^2-3x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow5x^3+9x^2+3x-1=0\\Rightarrow(x+1)^2(5x-1)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, i.e. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac15,-\\frac{24}{5}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{k}{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant. Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\dfrac12,2k\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=kx^{-1}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-kx^{-2},\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1/2}=-4k.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3+px^2+qx+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(2,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The gradient of the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1=8+4p+2q+5\\Rightarrow4p+2q=-12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2+2px+q.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"10=12+4p+q\\Rightarrow4p+q=-2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"p=2\\text{ and }q=-10.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The graph below shows the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=-x^2+2x+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which meets the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The tangent lines to the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> meet at point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the area of the triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.32/questions/assets/q14.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=-x^2+2x+8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{A}(-2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{B}(4,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=-2x+2,\\qquad f'(-2)=6.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-0=6(x+2)\\Rightarrow y=6x+12.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(4)=-6,\\quad y-0=-6(x-4)\\Rightarrow y=-6x+24.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"6x+12=-6x+24\\text{ so }12x=12\\Rightarrow x=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=6\\times1+12=18.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Area of triangle: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times6\\times18=54\\text{ units}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3+(1+p)x^2+qx+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. It passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(-1,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The gradient of the normal to the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"6=-1+(1+p)-q+5\\Rightarrow p-q=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2+2(1+p)x+q.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"-2=3-2(1+p)+q\\Rightarrow-2p+q=-3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"p=2\\text{ and }q=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x^3-5x^5+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> the tangent line has the same gradient as another tangent line to the curve. Find the equation of this other tangent line.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=-3+5+1=3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=3x^3-5x^5+1\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=9x^2-25x^4.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Gradient at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=-1}=-16\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"9x^2-25x^4=-16\\Rightarrow25x^4-9x^2-16=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(x-1)(x+1)(25x^2+16)=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3-5+1=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y+1=-16(x-1)\\Rightarrow y=-16x+15.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>Show that the equation of the tangent to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac1{x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a^3y+2x=3a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^{-2}\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-2x^{-3}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1{a^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-\\frac1{a^2}=-\\frac2{a^3}(x-a).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"a^3y-a=-2(x-a),\\quad a^3y-a=-2x+2a,\\quad a^3y+2x=3a.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q18","number":18,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the equation of the tangent to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x(x^2+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(3a^2+2)x-2a^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence explain why the gradient of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x(x^2+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is always positive.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^3+2x\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2+2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3a^2+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-(a^3+2a)=(3a^2+2)(x-a).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-a^3-2a=3a^2x-3a^3+2x-2a.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=(3a^2+2)x-2a^3.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for all real values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x^2+2&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for all real values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the gradient of the curve is always positive.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q19","number":19,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q19: Second derivatives</strong> A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2(1-kx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant. Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=x^2-kx^3\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x-3kx^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=2-6kx\\text{ so }\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=2}=2-12k.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q20","number":20,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q20--Q27: Differentiation of the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ae^{kx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> Evaluate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f'(1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for each of the following, leaving your answers in exact form:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=e^{6x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=\\sqrt{x}-e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=x^{4/3}+e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=6e^{6x}\\text{ so }f'(1)=6e^6.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=\\frac12x^{-1/2}-2e^{2x}\\text{ so }f'(1)=\\frac12-2e^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=\\frac43x^{1/3}+2e^{2x}\\text{ so }f'(1)=\\frac43+2e^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the tangent line to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^x,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=0}=1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-1=1(x-0)\\text{ so }y=x+1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the normal line to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2-e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x-2e^{2x},\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=0}=-2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y+1=\\frac12(x-0)\\text{ so }y=\\frac12x-1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q23","number":23,"question":"<p>The curve of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^x-2x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is shown on the diagram below. The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,e-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.32/questions/assets/q23.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the equation of the tangent line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants to be found.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates where the tangent line crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>Hence calculate the area of the triangle bounded by the tangent line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the coordinate axes giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{a}{b-e}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to find.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^x-4x,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=e-4.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-(e-2)=(e-4)(x-1).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=(e-4)x+(4-e)+e-2\\Rightarrow y=(e-4)x+2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(0,2)\\text{ and }\\left(-\\frac2{e-4},0\\right)=\\left(\\frac2{4-e},0\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times2\\times\\frac2{4-e}=\\frac2{4-e}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q24","number":24,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4e^{-kx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=k^2y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-4ke^{-kx},\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=2}=-4ke^{-2k}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=4k^2e^{-kx}=k^2y\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q25","number":25,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{5kx}(1-k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant. Given that at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\dfrac1k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=-100e^5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=e^{5kx}-ke^{5kx},\\quad\\frac{dy}{dx}=5ke^{5kx}-5k^2e^{5kx}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=25k^2e^{5kx}-25k^3e^{5kx}=25k^2e^{5kx}(1-k).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac1k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25k^2e^{5k\\times1/k}(1-k)=-100e^5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25k^2(1-k)=-100\\Rightarrow k^2-k^3=-4\\Rightarrow k^3-k^2-4=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(k-2)(k^2+k+2)=0\\text{ so }k=2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q26","number":26,"question":"<p>The curve of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x-e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is shown on the diagram below. The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,10-e^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.32/questions/assets/q26.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the equation of the normal line at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants to be found.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates where the normal line meet the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(e^4+ae^2+b,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are integers to be found.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=5-e^x,\\qquad\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=2}=5-e^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-(10-e^2)=\\frac1{e^2-5}(x-2).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow y=\\frac1{e^2-5}x-\\frac2{e^2-5}+10-e^2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left(0,-\\frac2{e^2-5}+10-e^2\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac2{e^2-5}-10+e^2=\\frac1{e^2-5}x.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x=2-10(e^2-5)+e^2(e^2-5)\\Rightarrow x=e^4-15e^2+52.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(e^4-15e^2+52,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.32-q27","number":27,"question":"<p>The normal to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)=e^x-2x^2-x+e^{-x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the same line as the tangent to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)=\\dfrac12x^2+(5+k)x+p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(7,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"f'(x)=e^x-4x-1-e^{-x}\\text{ so }f'(0)=-1.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-2=1(x-0)\\Rightarrow y=x+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"g(x)=\\frac12x^2+(5+k)x+p,\\quad g'(x)=x+5+k.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"g'(7)=1=12+k\\text{ so }k=-11\\Rightarrow g(x)=\\frac12x^2-6x+p.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(7,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9=\\frac{49}{2}-42+p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=26.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]}]